Texts (stories, explanations in research/ and content files): Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Quotes: the short quotes in the source lists come from the Historical Dictionary of Switzerland (Historisches Lexikon der Schweiz, HLS, https://hls-dhs-dss.ch) and other works. HLS texts are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/); each quote links to its article, and the quotes keep that licence. Our own texts are written in our own words from the facts in these sources.

Traced shapes: the areas in research/traced/ (used in the Romans story) are traced from HLS maps, so they are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 as well. Source maps: HLS articles 'Helvetier' and 'Römisches Reich' (https://hls-dhs-dss.ch).

Data:
- Lines and areas derived from OpenStreetMap: Open Database License (ODbL), (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
- Europe regions and countries: Natural Earth, public domain.
- Swiss borders: BFS GEOSTAT via swiss-maps, non-commercial use, attribute "Bundesamt für Statistik (BFS), GEOSTAT".
- Map tiles and historical maps: swisstopo (shown, not redistributed).
